            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="FOX03" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>William Johnson</forename>
                        <surname>Fox</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1786">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1864"/>
                    <occupation>Orator, Minister, South Place Chapel, editor of the Unitarian
                        Monthly Repository</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> On 18 November 1827, Godwin notes 'hear Fox' - it is a Sunday. In 1835,
                            one of the contacts is Fox (Finsbury), again on a Sunday, suggesting a
                            service. This, and the circles in which he encounters Fox after 1827
                            makes it likely that this is the Minister William Johnson Fox, who
                            played a major role in Unitarian circles. </p>
                        <p>See https://heritage.humanists.uk/william-johnson-fox/</p><p>DNB</p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
